prompt.en:
A search box writes to the URL on every keystroke: <pre>function Search() {
  const router = useRouter(), pathname = usePathname();
  return &lt;input onChange={(e) =&gt;
    router.push(`${pathname}?q=${e.target.value}`)} /&gt;;
}</pre> Users complain that the Back button "doesn't work" (it takes many presses to leave the page) and that typing feels laggy. Diagnose both symptoms in terms of what <code>router.push</code> does, then explain the right split of storage. Then self-check.

